1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,750
Satellite signals change pitch?

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,450
The cause: the Doppler shift.

3
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:05,350
Low-orbit satellites fly incredibly fast.

4
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:08,980
Approaching: the waves bunch up, the
frequency rises.

5
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,300
Overhead: the shift is zero.

6
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:13,770
Receding: the waves spread out, the
frequency drops.

7
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,410
At 2 GHz: close to ±50 kHz.

8
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:19,820
At 20 GHz: ten times more.

9
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:22,450
The orbit is known, so it can be computed
ahead.

10
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:24,650
Compensate in reverse: no more pitch
change.
